# Example environment for xebec.
#
#   cp example.env .env.local   # gitignored; edit that copy, never this file
#   npm run dev                 # http://localhost:5173
#
# Vite reads .env, .env.local, .env.[mode] and .env.[mode].local. Variables set in your shell
# take precedence, e.g. `MERIDIAN_URL=http://localhost:4001 npm run dev`.
#
# Everything here is optional. The defaults fit meridian running on localhost:4000.
#
# Meridian's own settings (upstream model server, admin token, CORS) live in meridian's
# example.env, not here. "No upstream is configured" means meridian's LLM_BASE_URL is unset.

## Development (npm run dev)

# Where the dev server proxies /api to. Default: http://localhost:4000
MERIDIAN_URL=http://localhost:4000

## Build (npm run build)

# Meridian's origin, baked into dist/ at build time. Unset (the default) means same origin:
# the dev proxy, or dist/ served behind a reverse proxy that routes /api to meridian.
# When set, add xebec's origin to meridian's CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS.
# VITE_MERIDIAN_URL=https://meridian.example.com
